          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "车票 — chēpiào — \"train or bus ticket\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "车票多少钱 chēpiào duōshao qián — How much is the ticket?"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The new character, in pieces: 票 (piào) — eleven strokes: on top a bar over a frame with two short verticals; under it 二, a hooked vertical and two dots. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "车票 (chēpiào) is built from 车 'vehicle' and 票 (piào) 'a ticket'. The first is inherited from Middle Chinese tsyhae (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription); no dictionary we use records an older form of the second, so its history is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
